//       - right-aligned broadcasting (size-1 dims stretch),
//       - C-order flatten / reshape / ravel,
//       - astype float->int is trunc-toward-zero (static_cast),
//       - true-division always promotes to double,
//       - reductions accumulate in fixed C-order (NO reordering) so results are
//         deterministic under -O2 IEEE math (never build with -ffast-math).
//   * The library NEVER reorders floating-point reductions or uses BLAS — the
//     parity tolerances (1e-4 scalar / 1e-3 geo-IK) depend on this.
//
// Dtype policy: nd::Array is templated on the element type. The transpiler's
// type/shape lattice picks T and inserts astype<>() casts, so each op here is
// within-dtype; cross-dtype arithmetic is the transpiler's job, not this file's.

